{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0112"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c010): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c010.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0112"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/film","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/film-media__film.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",832],["+","The quietest member of the family was played by John Cazale (1935–1978): Fredo, the weak, overlooked middle brother who betrays Michael in “The Godfather Part II” and pays for it with his life. Cazale made only five feature films before he died of cancer at 42 – “The Godfather”, “The Conversation”, “The Godfather Part II”, “Dog Day Afternoon” and “The Deer Hunter” – and every one of them was nominated for the Oscar for Best Picture; three of them won.\n\n"],["=",278],["+","John Cazale | Fredo Corleone | Never nominated; all five of his films Best Picture nominees |\n| "],["=",25]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",772],["+","Das stillste Familienmitglied spielte John Cazale (1935–1978): Fredo, den schwachen, übergangenen mittleren Bruder, der Michael in „Der Pate – Teil II“ verrät und dafür mit dem Leben bezahlt. Cazale drehte nur fünf Spielfilme, bevor er mit 42 Jahren an Krebs starb – „Der Pate“, „Der Dialog“, „Der Pate – Teil II“, „Hundstage“ und „Die durch die Hölle gehen“ –, und jeder davon war für den Oscar als bester Film nominiert; drei gewannen ihn.\n\n"],["=",264],["+","John Cazale | Fredo Corleone | Nie nominiert; alle fünf seiner Filme als bester Film nominiert |\n| "],["=",23]]}]},
